course: dictionary
lesson: 746
title: What is a bathroom?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bathroom is a room with a bath or shower, a washbasin and usually a toilet. When you meet the word, look for these three things in the sentence or picture around it.
explain: In the USA and Canada, «bathroom» is also a polite word for any toilet, even one with no bath. So «May I go to the bathroom?» means May I use the toilet? The words around it show which meaning fits.
explain: Bathrooms are also places where you must be careful. The sentence «Little children should not lock the bathroom door» tells you that grown-ups need to be able to get in if someone is ill or stuck.
fact: A bathroom is a room with a bath or shower, a washbasin and usually a toilet.
fact: In the USA and Canada, «bathroom» can mean any toilet, even one with no bath.
fact: Wet bathroom floors are slippery, so walk carefully.
fact: Medicines and cleaning products must be locked away, often in the bathroom cabinet.
fact: «Bathroom» is a noun: one bathroom, two bathrooms.
exercise: «The bathroom has its own good habits: your own toothbrush, the toilet lid down, hot hair tools switched off and the fan on after a steamy bath.» Name one good habit in the bathroom. | *Using your own toothbrush | Leaving the fan off after a steamy bath | Sharing a toothbrush with a friend | Leaving hot hair tools switched on
exercise: «Knock on a closed bathroom door and wait, and others should do the same for you.» What should you do before you go into a closed bathroom? | Shout through the keyhole | Push the door open quickly | *Knock and wait | Unlock it with a hairpin
exercise: Which of these is a danger in a bathroom? | A clean towel on the rail | Soap in a dish | *Electric things used near water | A toothbrush in a cup
test: In the USA and Canada, what does «May I go to the bathroom?» mean? | May I wash my hair? | May I take a bath? | May I brush my teeth? | *May I use the toilet?
test: Why must small children never be left alone in the bath? | They will want a longer bath | It saves water | *It is dangerous to leave them alone | The water gets cold too quickly
exam: In «Example: in a bathroom with no window, steam has nowhere to go.», why does steam stay in the room? | *Because there is no window for it to escape through | Because the fan is always switched on | Because bathrooms have no doors | Because steam only forms in kitchens
